From 6d294b8feb745656d6e96c9e19e116f607d900be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-base <nixos-base@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:31:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Live "shader:" wallpaper (phase 1: single pass)

Runs Shadertoy-style GLSL fragment shaders (mainImage(), the Shadertoy
uniforms, the KDE Shader Wallpaper plugin's iScreenOffset and
iDesktopResolution) as a live wallpaper through the LiveWallpaperSource
interface. Design: docs/shader-wallpaper-design.md.

- "shader:<name>" looks the shader up in [wallpaper.shader] directories,
  then $XDG_DATA_HOME and $XDG_DATA_DIRS (noctalia/shaders): <spec>,
  <spec>.frag, Shaders/<spec>.frag, <library>/Shaders/<spec>.frag.
  Absolute or "~" paths are used as they are.
- One GL program per path, shared by the desktop and lock surfaces, with a
  render target per (consumer, path). fragCoord is passed flipped, so the
  texture stores the top row first without a copy; shaders with their own
  main() are flipped by a blit.
- Compiles on first use (a one-time hitch), with a program binary cache in
  $XDG_CACHE_HOME/noctalia/shaders.
- desktop_fps / lock_fps caps, render_scale (default 0.5), speed, and
  desktop/lock motion animated|still (still: one frame at still_time).
- A still per shader (2 s of iTime after it loads, or the still frame) for
  theme colours, the backdrop and the greeter.
- Hot reload when the file changes (checked once a second while
  animating). A missing or broken shader logs once, shows the fill colour,
  and is retried when the file changes or appears.
- iChannel0-3 are bound to black with iChannelResolution 0 (phase 2 adds
  textures).

Tests: shader_source_test (path syntax, lookup order, uniform injection,
own-main() shaders). Headless: 192/194 phase-1 KDE shaders compile on the
RTX 4090. In a nested Umbriel: correct orientation, animation on the
desktop and lock screen, still mode, hot reload, binary-cache hit after a
restart, fill-colour fallback for missing and broken shaders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
