From 7b313f5cebb0860254fe9fe126e7dd4929f06225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-base <nixos-base@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:42:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Shader wallpaper: channel textures (phase 2)

iChannel0-3 now read images:
- A shader's header directives, as in KDE Shader Wallpaper (first 60 lines):
  "// @texture0 Resources/x.jpg" (relative to the library root, the parent
  of a Shaders/ directory, then beside the shader) and
  "// @channels tex0, none, audio, bufferA" (routing per channel; without
  it, iChannelN reads slot N).
- [wallpaper.shader.textures] "<spec>:<slot>" = "path" overrides a slot,
  for shaders that leave their channels to the user.

Images are decoded once and shared by every program (longer edge at most
2048 px), mipmapped and repeating, and uploaded bottom row first
(Shadertoy's vflip), with iChannelResolution set. Audio and buffer channels
log once and read black until phase 3. Changing the overrides reloads the
shaders and retries images that failed.

Tests: directive parsing (tokens, defaults, 60-line limit, CRLF) and
texture path lookup. All 53 texture-only KDE shaders compile. Headless:
texture orientation and iChannelResolution checked with a test image, and
Abstract_Plane, Circuits, Cloud_Fairies and CubeLines (via an override)
render with their images.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
