From b49a95a947cc4a35dcb796d2d92f9bc5e0fcad4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-base <nixos-base@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:07:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Shader wallpaper: buffer passes and background compiles
 (phase 3)

Multi-pass shaders: <stem>_bufferA-D.frag run before the image pass, with
Shadertoy's Common code (<stem>_common.frag, plus the main file's
"const ...; // @shared" lines, as in KDE Shader Wallpaper).

- Routing follows the plugin. Without directives, the image reads buffer
  A on iChannel0 and each buffer reads itself. A buffer file's @channels
  wins over the main file's; "self", bufferA-D and 10-13 are accepted.
- clamp(round(dt * 240), 1, 8) substeps per frame, with iSubstep and
  iSubsteps; "@substeps 1" passes run once, on the last substep.
  "@sim-max-height N" caps the buffer rows.
- Buffers are RGBA32F (falling back to 16F, then 8), cleared to zero, and
  kept across frames; they reset on resize or a new build. Each buffer
  reads its previous step; other readers get its latest output. Buffer
  passes read buffers NEAREST, the image pass LINEAR (sampler objects).
- iTimeDelta is now the iTime since that target's previous frame (it
  was the last tick's step).
- KDE's window and desktop uniforms (iWindowRects, iWindowCount,
  iVirtualDesktop*, iMousePrev) are declared so its window-reactive
  shaders compile; they read no windows and one desktop.

Background compiles: KDE's neko takes 27 s to compile on the RTX 4090.
Programs now build through GL_KHR_parallel_shader_compile and are polled
from frameTexture() (frames keep coming while anything compiles); a
binary-cache hit is ready at once. Drivers without the extension keep the
synchronous path.

Fix: a render target was recreated every frame. Recreation reset its
idle stamp, so releaseRetired() freed it again on the next frame. This
was harmless for stateless shaders but made buffers restart every frame.

Tests: routing defaults and precedence, buffer and common file
discovery, the @shared split, substep counts, simulation size. All 18
non-audio buffer shaders compile with their passes. Headless: a feedback
shader accumulates about 257 steps/s at 30 fps; falling_sand,
rainy_window, fireflies and neko animate; the shell answered IPC in
about 80 ms during neko's 25 s background compile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
