From eb8be4dc3d14a0b1f73e08622c4a4105efc53d51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-base <nixos-base@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:07:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Shader thumbnails: render single-pass shaders without
 waiting

noctalia-shader-thumbnail waited 1.5 s of real time per shader before
reading a frame. Single-pass shaders depend only on iTime, so they now
render in still motion at iTime = --time and are read as soon as they
compile. Only shaders with _bufferA-D passes, whose state builds up over
frames, still run animated for --time seconds, after the others.
ShaderLiveWallpaper::hasBufferPasses() tells the two apart.

